{{!--
  Favicon (GH-114). `site.keys.favicon` is a playbook-level override — same
  convention as `site.keys.productLogo` in nav-brand.hbs and `site.keys.repoUrl`
  in repo-link.hbs — a root-relative or absolute URL to an icon image, set in
  the playbook as `site.keys.favicon`. Absent, no `<link rel="icon">` is
  emitted at all and the browser falls back to its own default (or whatever a
  previous crawl cached), rather than pointing at an asset the bundle does not
  ship. `relativize`, not root-absolute: this is an ordinary `<link href>`
  resolved against the current document, the same as every other bundle asset
  reference except home-background's CSS custom property — see head-styles.hbs
  for why that one is the exception, not the rule.
--}}
{{#with site.keys.favicon}}
    <link rel="icon" href="{{{relativize this}}}">
{{/with}}
